# Sixty-four cells that are nominally identical and physically are not.
#
# Every cell gets the same knobs. They behave differently anyway: at 6%
# tolerance each one draws its own capacitance, recovery rate, threshold and
# saturation, and each has its own noise stream. The bank starts in step
# because it starts from the same state, then drifts apart.
#
# TC-3 watches three slices of the bank and feeds its mixed output back into
# all of them, so the cells are weakly coupled through a connectome that is
# itself changing. Watch brain.norm: synaptic scaling holds the total
# conductance near its target while the individual routes move.
#
#   kaukonen render --patch patches/bank64.kpatch --html out/bank64.html --stride 20
#
# The raster pane in that page is the point. All 64 cells fire together for the
# first few hundred milliseconds, because they start from the same state. Then
# tolerance and noise pull them apart - and they do not simply scatter: the weak
# coupling keeps gathering them back into partial groups of twenty to forty,
# indefinitely, without ever returning to lockstep. Individual cells fire
# between 17 and 39 times over the twenty seconds.

dt 0.0005
seconds 20
seed 2024
mismatch 0.06

module cells rc1[64] preset=burst noise=0.02 drift=0.01 output_gain=2.5
module brain tc3     rule=oja gamma=0.5 scaling=0.8 target_norm=1.0 activity_gain=0.01 drift=0.005
# The cells rest at a strongly negative output, so summing them would be a
# large negative bias that suppresses the whole bank. The offset re-centres
# the coupling, and the attenuator keeps it weak enough to stay interesting.
module fan   mix     a0=0.08 a1=0 a2=0 a3=0 offset=0.5

# Three slices of the bank, so the connectome sees three different populations.
patch cells[0].out  -> brain.a
patch cells[1].out  -> brain.a
patch cells[2].out  -> brain.a
patch cells[21].out -> brain.b
patch cells[22].out -> brain.b
patch cells[23].out -> brain.b
patch cells[42].out -> brain.c
patch cells[43].out -> brain.c
patch cells[44].out -> brain.c

# Its own plasticity is the learning signal, and the mixed output is the only
# thing coupling the cells to each other.
patch brain.activity -> brain.learn
patch brain.a -> fan.in0
patch fan.out -> cells[*].in

record cells[*].v brain.w00 brain.w11 brain.w22 brain.norm brain.activity
